      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i'm an architect working in a high-rise dev in NYC and i've been noticing something weird with the HVAC and smart lighting cycles. there's this low-frequency hum, like maybe sub-audible? i can't exactly hear it but i feel it in my chest and it's making me super restless/anxious. do you know if there are specific frequencies used in smart building systems that could cause this kind of physiological response?",
